{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792496478,"nonce":"1re7RfYoMH+JX3Yr1LRIL2ir/zo=","message":"Measured embedded extension opens on main at 99d38d4, pinned Ashui 61510d37b56ad3ee938f175f5feb9916ad4b526a, Ash 1e95e1978118d73bd083d04556441070f669c7fd and RayScript 555ee9a09095dc2b8eba21011d7c84b4ade6491c. macOS arm64; GPU offscreen rendering at 1280x800, without PNG readback; GC root/stat logging unset. Other Rust builds caused wall-time variance, so first-open fixture numbers are medians of three fresh processes. Native and hybrid programs use the same view code, fixture and shared libraries.\n\nReady time / longest uninterrupted UI turn, milliseconds (hybrid; AOT):\n- Sidebar: 346 / 346; 56 / 56.\n- Expanded graph: 210 / 102; 147 / 75.\n- Small Markdown with math, Mermaid, highlighting and SVG: 522 / 281; 303 / 172.\n- RayDE README with its local SVG/PNG assets, one run each: 623 / 453; 552 / 458.\n- 7,838-byte Markdown containing eight copies of the rich fixture, one run each: 1946 / 1435; 1570 / 1136. Reopening the retained parsed document: 1218 ms hybrid, 1120 ms AOT, with no Markdown VM rendering.\n\nVM graph pump turns were roughly 1-2 ms; the initial Git startup pump can be much longer on its own worker. Small Markdown native rendering was 79-269 ms cold and 45-54 ms warm; the larger document took 381-438 ms on its worker. No transport.poll call exceeded the timing logger's 1 ms threshold. Durations overlap and must not be added together.\n\nNative stack sample during AOT large-Markdown reactivation: all 731 main-thread samples were beneath LayoutTree.computeLayout -\u003e hl_blinc_tree_compute_layout in blinc_abi.hdll. Both rayde-extension threads were waiting on their input channels throughout those samples; GC worker threads were also parked. This identifies synchronous UI/native layout as a recurring blocker without blaming the RayScript scheduler. It does not reproduce the literal 3-second pointer spin in a windowed app.\n\nMarkdownView rebuilds every block synchronously on activation, including offscreen CodeViews, math and diagrams. Image residency only controls decoded image data. Also scm.rays refreshes status, history, refs and selected-commit files for every active.changed event, generating hundreds of operations when switching tabs even if Git data did not change.\n\nArtifacts: bin/extension-{hybrid,aot}/summary.json and results.json, bin/extension-readme-{hybrid,aot}/, bin/extension-stress-{hybrid,aot}/, and bin/extension-stress-stack/sample.txt (with ui.log and worker.log). Initial failed exploratory parser/inspector runs were excluded; the repeat runner uses separate worker and UI logs.\n\nAdded scripts/extension-bench.sh (and --native), tests/ExtensionProbe.hx, tests/extension_probe.py and opt-in RAYDE_EXTENSION_TIMING=1 stage logging. Core compiler/extension integration checks passed. The user's scripts/deps.sh pin change is preserved outside this change. No visual behavior changes or extra Cargo target directories.","files":null}]}